      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 5.2,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture we learned about property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.2,
          "end": 8.1,
          "en": "Now, if we had the use case that we also want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.1,
          "end": 11.451,
          "en": "output the current value of allow you new server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.451,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "we could of course use string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 16.65,
          "en": "to simply output allow a new server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.65,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "and a bullion can also be cast into a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 21.57,
          "en": "So now we see false here and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 23.22,
          "en": "after two seconds you see this change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.22,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "to true because we change it in the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "Nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "Now this is one of the cases here where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 31.83,
          "en": "you can easily use property binding instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.83,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "of string interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 35.573,
          "en": "So you could simply bind to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.573,
          "end": 40.573,
          "en": "property of this element, the inner text property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "and set this equal to allow a new server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 47.31,
          "en": "Now I can remove the string interpolation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 48.63,
          "en": "inside of the text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.63,
          "end": 50.619,
          "en": "And whilst it might look empty now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.619,
          "end": 52.29,
          "en": "while we set the inner text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.29,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "so we get the same behavior as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 57.488,
          "en": "because the inner text property of element is just what's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.488,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "between the opening and closing tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 63.567,
          "en": "So in this case, we were able to easily replace string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.567,
          "end": 65.88,
          "en": "and interpolation with property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.88,
          "end": 68.44800000000001,
          "en": "So when should you use which of the two?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.44800000000001,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "Well, basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "if you want to output something in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 74.779,
          "en": "print some text to it, use string and interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.779,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "If you want to change some property, be that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 82.53,
          "en": "of an HTML element or as you later learn off a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "or a component, typically use property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "That is how you can differentiate it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 89.189,
          "en": "and you will get a feeling for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.189,
          "end": 92.90899999999999,
          "en": "once you work your way through the course project and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.90899999999999,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "So this is this one important note I want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 100.995,
          "en": "make is don't mix property binding and string interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.995,
          "end": 104.699,
          "en": "You might notice that here we have disabled equals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.699,
          "end": 106.669,
          "en": "and then we have quotation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.669,
          "end": 109.916,
          "en": "and then directly our property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.916,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "There are no curly braces between these quotation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "and there shouldn't be because that will break the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 118.517,
          "en": "This will not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.517,
          "end": 121.608,
          "en": "between the quotation marks of property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.608,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "You can and you must already write TypeScript codes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 128.16,
          "en": "so to say, a TypeScript expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.16,
          "end": 131.01,
          "en": "which will return the value this property expects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.01,
          "end": 131.88,
          "en": "So for disabled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.88,
          "end": 134.28,
          "en": "some expression which returns true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.28,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "So just like with string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "you may also call a method there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 140.949,
          "en": "but you must not add curly braces in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.949,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "Once it might look, we simply use a HTML attribute there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 147.688,
          "en": "We aren't this whole syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.688,
          "end": 150.276,
          "en": "is a syntax recognized by angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.276,
          "end": 152.808,
          "en": "So this is why between the quotation marks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.808,
          "end": 155.048,
          "en": "you can already and you have already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.048,
          "end": 157.448,
          "en": "you have to write TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 157.448,
          "end": 160.5,
          "en": "because again, this whole expression is evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 160.5,
          "end": 164.109,
          "en": "by angular mixing in string interpolation will break it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.109,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "String interpolation only works in a normal template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 171.397,
          "en": "not within another expression of that template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.397,
          "end": 175.437,
          "en": "not within property binding or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.437,
          "end": 177.93,
          "en": "With that, enough about property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 181.637,
          "en": "and generally about outputting data in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.637,
          "end": 185.823,
          "en": "Let's see how we can react to events.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
